A||N||12||DaRkLoRD||If there's one thing I've learned......||||9||
Z||000000||DaRkLoRD||12-06-2001||05:14 PM||||it's don't put important things off.<P>Carpe Diem. so easy to remember. so why do I keep screwing up by putting things off?<BR>for example.. a girl I really liked.. I waited too long to tell her how I felt about her, and by that time she's met someone else. Or not visiting an ill relative, while they're still alive..<P>I wonder how many more of my projects or inventions will be worthless because I didn't finish them on time, and someone else did a similar one before I got mine done (therefore looking as if I'd copied them) It's happened several times already on the forum, ideas I had but lacked the resources to do them. Also happened with a computer game, I made the mistake of discussing it with people on a programming chat. a year later someone else had produced and sold a game that had the same plot!<P>Anyway, if you want to do something.. do it. The alternative is spending most of your time regretting the things you never did.<P>and believe me, it's no fun.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||9
Z||000001||BN Boomer||12-06-2001||05:19 PM||||No matter what, you'll always look back with a certain amount of wist and regret when seeing things that you could have done better, opportunities you failed to grasp, wondering how things might have turned out if only you had.....<P>Just do the best you can at the time, be happy with what you have achieved, and never quit trying.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||stimpy||12-06-2001||06:07 PM||||It is far better to regret the things you've done then to regret the things you haven't done.||||reg||12
Z||000003||hugh||12-06-2001||06:15 PM||||Stimpy,You have said more in one sentence than I could have said in a paragraph.I agree 100%.||||reg||14
Z||000004||Sage||12-06-2001||06:24 PM||||Good lesson Steve!<P>"Of all the things that can be said, the saddest is, it could have been."<P>Don't know who's quote that is, so can't give credit, but it sure is true.<P>It's been said of regrets, that they should be for things done that maybe shouldn't have been, rather than things not done that should have been.<P>Disclaimer: Procrastination does NOT prolong life!<P>Hang in there Steve, you are very young.<P>Just get busy from where you are, nobody can go back!<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Have a good one!||||reg||1
Z||000005||Pyric||12-06-2001||06:40 PM||||You've got to live like you drive.<P>Foot on the gas... Eyes straight ahead... Full concentration... NEVER look back.  <P>If you're too busy looking back... you could jeopardize your future.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Mach10||12-06-2001||06:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pyric:<BR><B>You've got to live like you drive.<P>Foot on the gas... Eyes straight ahead... Full concentration... NEVER look back.  <P>If you're too busy looking back... you could jeopardize your future.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>OR... Foot on gas, headlights off, and hands off the steering wheel  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>||||reg||6
Z||000007||DaRkLoRD||12-06-2001||07:52 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pyric:<BR><B>You've got to live like you drive.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>pedal to the floor, 30 over the limit, with the occasional smoking burnout?<P>wow, that kind of life might be fun. LOL.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>    <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||12
Z||000008||BN Boomer||12-06-2001||08:33 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pyric:<BR><B>You've got to live like you drive.<P>Foot on the gas... Eyes straight ahead... Full concentration... NEVER look back.  <P>If you're too busy looking back... you could jeopardize your future.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>So what happens when you change lanes and fail to see that 18 wheeler passing you?<P>Sorry, but if you NEVER look back, you'll never learn from your mistakes. Those who fail to learn from history are doomed to repeat it. <P>||||reg||1
Z||000009||BN Boomer||12-06-2001||08:37 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by stimpy:<BR><B>It is far better to regret the things you've done then to regret the things you haven't done.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>While there is a great amount of truth in that, unfortunately, NONE of us has all the time necessary to explore every possible option in life.<P>I live a pretty full, comfortable life and am very content with the manner in which it has unfolded thus far, but there are those times when I wonder what may have been had I had a little better foresight in my younger years regarding things both done and left undone.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||Pyric||12-06-2001||08:47 PM||||My point was that if you spend all your time looking back, or even too much time looking back, you can not only repeat your mistake... but create a new one that is even worse.<P>It wasn't that you don't learn from them, you just don't focus on them.<P>For example, while driving, you can look in the rearview to examine the current situation, but if you do it for more than a second, any number of things could jump out in front of you and BOOM... you're history.<P>I think it would be a little better to repeat a mistake because you were looking toward the future than to be so enveloped in the past that you LOSE your future.<P>It's all relative, and I'd rather be around to make mistakes.  The knowledge gained from them wont do me much good otherwise.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Cooter||12-06-2001||09:16 PM||||From former President Richard M. Nixon:<BR>The saddest thing is not to have tried and failed, but to have failed to try.||||reg||1
Z||000012||BN Boomer||12-06-2001||09:47 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Pyric:<BR><B>My point was that if you spend all your time looking back, or even too much time looking back, you can not only repeat your mistake... but create a new one that is even worse.<P>It wasn't that you don't learn from them, you just don't focus on them.<P>For example, while driving, you can look in the rearview to examine the current situation, but if you do it for more than a second, any number of things could jump out in front of you and BOOM... you're history.<P>I think it would be a little better to repeat a mistake because you were looking toward the future than to be so enveloped in the past that you LOSE your future.<P>It's all relative, and I'd rather be around to make mistakes.  The knowledge gained from them wont do me much good otherwise.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I can agree with that. It's just that in your first reply I thought you put a little too much emphasis on NEVER looking back. One shouldn't focus on their past, but one also shouldn't forget where they came from, how they got where they are, and the lessons learned along the way.<P>||||reg||1
